  "description": "Run SQL on any ADO.NET connection and get the rows back as strongly typed objects (ExecuteQuery<T>, ExecuteQueryAsync<T>) or as dynamic objects (ExecuteQuery, ExecuteQueryAsync), streamed as IEnumerable<T> or IAsyncEnumerable<T>. The methods extend DbConnection and DbCommand; ExecuteCommand and ExecuteCommandAsync run statements that return no rows. Parameters are written as {{name}} in the SQL and always sent as real database parameters, never concatenated into it. Their values come from an anonymous object, a dictionary, a JsonElement or JSON text, and the delimiters can be changed. Typed results map columns to properties by name, or by [DataMember] or [JsonPropertyName]. JSON and XML columns can be returned as nested objects. Works with SQL Server, PostgreSQL, MySQL and MariaDB, SQLite, Oracle, DB2 and any other ADO.NET provider; on ODBC and OleDb the named parameters become positional ? parameters automatically. No package dependencies on .NET 8 and later. Targets .NET 10, 9 and 8, and .NET Standard 2.0, which includes .NET Framework 4.6.1 and later.",
