  "readmeFile": "nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Three fixes. 1) An error raised after the first result set (SQL Server THROW or RAISERROR after a SELECT, or a later statement that fails) is now thrown once the caller has read every row; closing the reader used to discard it. A caller that stops reading early still doesn't see it. Only the first result set is returned, as before. 2) A single column with no name (SQL Server COUNT(*) without an alias) returns one bare value per row (null for NULL, and default(T) for NULL in typed ExecuteQuery<T>); it used to return each row twice, and a NULL three times. 3) ExecuteCommand and ExecuteCommandAsync honour closeConnectionOnExit: they close the connection, without disposing it, also when the first statement fails. They also dispose the command they create.",
